outline.prompt:
Write a script outline for:
  title: {title}
  logline: {logline}
  genre/tone: {genre}

Structure it as a three-act outline in Markdown: Act headings, then a numbered list of plot beats/scenes under each act, each beat one to three sentences stating what happens, who it happens to, and where. Number every beat sequentially across the whole document (Beat 1, Beat 2, ...) so later stages can reference them unambiguously.

Emit as ONE path-bearing fence at {workspace}/outline.md. No other commentary outside the fence.

script.prompt:
Write the full script for "{title}" in standard script format (scene headings in caps, action lines in present tense, character cues centered in caps above dialogue, parentheticals sparingly).

OUTLINE:
{outline_doc}

SCENE CARDS (one scene per outline beat — cover every one, in order):
{scene_cards_text}

CHARACTER BIBLE (stay consistent with these voices and motivations):
{characters_doc}

LOCATIONS:
{locations_doc}

Emit the complete script as ONE path-bearing fence at {workspace}/script.md. No other commentary outside the fence.
